> What I am trying to achieve is to compare whether the latent variance differs across the two groups. How can I accomplish this?

Latent variance of what, intercept or slope (or both)?  As I suggested before, you can use labels to constrain parameters, as seen in the lavaan tutorial <http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/groups.html> (look in the section "Constraining a single parameter to be equal across groups" halfway down the page).  After fitting a model without the constraints (mod1) and a model with the constraints (mod0, which is nested within mod1), you can test the null hypothesis that the constraints hold by using the anova() function:  anova(mod1, mod0)

Terry

