> I am going to do a one-level SEM, just looking at if the gender (male or female) would also have some contributions to the dependent variable. So I just wonder if Lavaan can do this one level, or just how to code this path in the lavann package?

You can create a dummy code (e.g., 1 = female, 0 = male) to represent gender, then include it as a predictor in your model.  See the tutorial for how to specify regression paths:

http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/syntax1.html

